What:		/sys/bus/platform/devices/1100b000.thermal/hw_critical_temp
Date:		October 2026
Contact:	X20 Bring-up <admin@taterli.com>
Description:
		Read/write the six-bank TC final direct-reset threshold in
		millidegrees Celsius. Default follows the board's critical trip
		(150000); allowed writes are 10000..150000. Thresholds use BSP
		eFuse/AUXADC calibration. TC drives TOPRGU directly, without a
		software IRQ actuator; the driver also establishes the BSP external
		reset and bypass-power-key flags. A low test threshold can reset
		the board immediately. Writes are transient and do not edit DT.
		This is separate from the normal passive thermal cooling policy
		and the BIG PID frequency cap. Reading it does not prove a real
		150 C action, physical power-off or subsequent boot recovery.
